# Trivy ignore list for the release runtime images.
#
# Deliberate, reviewed HIGH/CRITICAL waivers only. Every entry names a concrete,
# justified reason; anything without one must be fixed, not ignored. The
# release-candidate workflow scans os,library vulns at HIGH,CRITICAL with
# --ignore-unfixed, so only fixable findings ever reach this list.
#
# Review by: 2026-12-01
#
# --- Build-tool package metadata, not a runtime code path -------------------
# The scanner/api images uninstall setuptools and msgpack as non-runtime build
# tools (see scanner/Dockerfile: `pip uninstall -y --break-system-packages
# msgpack setuptools` and the pip removal that follows), but Trivy still detects
# leftover dist-info metadata for them. No shipped runtime module imports either
# package, so these HIGH findings describe metadata, not exploitable code. The
# genuinely runtime-vendored grpc finding (CVE-2026-84304) is FIXED in the image
# instead, by building the Go tools against grpc >= 1.83.1.
CVE-2025-47273
GHSA-6v7p-g79w-8964
